        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add accessibility note for screen reader support to ElementInternals.labels]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45208</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45208"/>
        <updated>2026-08-18T03:03:13.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258725120?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h2 dir="auto">Description</h2>
<p dir="auto">This adds an Accessibility section to the <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ElementInternals/labels" rel="nofollow">ElementInternals.labels</a> page, documenting that screen reader support for labels associated via  varies by browser.</p>
<p dir="auto">Key points covered:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>In most browsers, the label is announced when the custom element receives focus</li>
<li>Safari does not reliably narrate labels associated via  for form-associated custom elements (referencing <a href="https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=259124" rel="nofollow">WebKit bug 259124</a>)</li>
<li>Developers should consider supplementing with ARIA attributes (, ) for robust cross-browser support</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #44395.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4621852846" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44395" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/44395/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/44395">#44395</a></p>]]></content>
