        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF155 supports web rtc error events with the <code class="notranslate">sctp-error</code> type fired at a data channel with <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError/errorDetail" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">RTCError.errorDetail</code></a> set to <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError/errorDetail#sctp-failure" rel="nofollow">"sctp-failure"</a> in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1814460</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">This adds the release note. Note that <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCErrorEvent" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">RTCErrorEvent</code></a> and its <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RTCError" rel="nofollow"><code class="notranslate">RTCError</code></a> property are also supported on dedicated workers so this is mentioned (it is non-standard nowm, but coming to the spec).</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="5170074351" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/45175/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/45175">#45175</a></p>]]></content>
